  "id": "escapism",
  "term": "escapism",
  "definition": "Escapism is the use of gaming as a way to get psychological relief or to mentally get away from real-life concerns. In mental health research, it is described as a major motive for gaming that can be linked with either helpful outcomes or problematic gaming, depending in part on how well a person shifts back to everyday life after play.",
